"Tutorial sobre el uso de curses con Python, por Andrew Kuchling y Eric "
"Raymond."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:53
msgid "Functions"
msgstr "Funciones"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:55
msgid "The module :mod:`!curses` defines the following exception:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:60
msgid "Exception raised when a curses library function returns an error."
msgstr ""
"Excepción lanzada cuando una función de la biblioteca curses devuelve un "
"error."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:64
msgid ""
"Whenever *x* or *y* arguments to a function or a method are optional, they "
"default to the current cursor location. Whenever *attr* is optional, it "
"defaults to :const:`A_NORMAL`."
msgstr ""
"Siempre que los argumentos *x* o *y* de una función o un método sean "
"opcionales, se situarán por defecto en la posición actual del cursor. Cuando "
"*attr* es opcional, su valor por defecto es :const:`A_NORMAL`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:68
msgid "The module :mod:`!curses` defines the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:73
msgid ""
"Allow use of default values for colors on terminals supporting this feature. "
"Use this to support transparency in your application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:76
msgid ""
"Assign terminal default foreground/background colors to color number ``-1``. "
"So ``init_pair(x, COLOR_RED, -1)`` will initialize pair *x* as red on "
"default background and ``init_pair(x, -1, COLOR_BLUE)`` will initialize pair "
"*x* as default foreground on blue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:81
msgid "Change the definition of the color-pair ``0`` to ``(fg, bg)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:83
msgid "This is an ncurses extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:90
msgid ""
"Return the output speed of the terminal in bits per second.  On software "
"terminal emulators it will have a fixed high value. Included for historical "
"reasons; in former times, it was used to  write output loops for time delays "
"and occasionally to change interfaces depending on the line speed."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve la velocidad de salida del terminal en bits por segundo.  En "
"emuladores de terminal por software tendrá un valor alto fijo. Incluido por "
"razones históricas; antiguamente se utilizaba para escribir bucles de salida "
"para retardos y ocasionalmente para cambiar de interfaz en función de la "
"velocidad de la línea."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:98
msgid "Emit a short attention sound."
msgstr "Emite un breve sonido de atención."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:103
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` or ``False``, depending on whether the programmer can change "
"the colors displayed by the terminal."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` o ``False``, dependiendo de si el programador puede "
"cambiar los colores mostrados por el terminal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:109
msgid ""
"Enter cbreak mode.  In cbreak mode (sometimes called \"rare\" mode) normal "
"tty line buffering is turned off and characters are available to be read one "
"by one. However, unlike raw mode, special characters (interrupt, quit, "
"suspend, and flow control) retain their effects on the tty driver and "
"calling program.  Calling first :func:`raw` then :func:`cbreak` leaves the "
"terminal in cbreak mode."
msgstr ""
"Entra en el modo cbreak.  En el modo cbreak (a veces llamado modo \"raro\") "
"el búfer de línea normal de tty se desactiva y los caracteres están "
"disponibles para ser leídos uno a uno. Sin embargo, a diferencia del modo "
"raw, los caracteres especiales (interrupción, abandono, suspensión y control "
"de flujo) conservan sus efectos sobre el controlador tty y el programa de "
"llamada.  Llamar primero a :func:`raw` y luego a :func:`cbreak` deja el "
"terminal en modo cbreak."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:118
msgid ""
"Return the intensity of the red, green, and blue (RGB) components in the "
"color *color_number*, which must be between ``0`` and ``COLORS - 1``.  "
"Return a 3-tuple, containing the R,G,B values for the given color, which "
"will be between ``0`` (no component) and ``1000`` (maximum amount of "
"component).  Raise an exception if the color is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:127
msgid ""
"Return the attribute value for displaying text in the specified color pair. "
"Only the first 256 color pairs are supported. This attribute value can be "
"combined with :const:`A_STANDOUT`, :const:`A_REVERSE`, and the other :const:"
"`!A_\\*` attributes.  :func:`pair_number` is the counterpart to this "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el valor del atributo para mostrar texto en el par de colores "
"especificado. Sólo se admiten los 256 primeros pares de colores. Este valor "
"de atributo puede combinarse con :const:`A_STANDOUT`, :const:`A_REVERSE`, y "
"los demás atributos :const:`!A_\\*`. :func:`pair_number` es la contrapartida "
"de esta función."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:136
msgid ""
"Set the cursor state.  *visibility* can be set to ``0``, ``1``, or ``2``, "
"for invisible, normal, or very visible.  If the terminal supports the "
"visibility requested, return the previous cursor state; otherwise raise an "
"exception.  On many terminals, the \"visible\" mode is an underline cursor "
"and the \"very visible\" mode is a block cursor."
msgstr ""
"Establece el estado del cursor.  *visibility* puede definirse como ``0``, "
"``1``, o ``2``, para invisible, normal o muy visible.  Si el terminal "
"soporta la visibilidad solicitada, devuelve el estado anterior del cursor; "
"en caso contrario, lanza una excepción.  En muchos terminales, el modo "
"\"visible\" es un cursor subrayado y el modo \"muy visible\" es un cursor de "
"bloque."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:145
msgid ""
"Save the current terminal mode as the \"program\" mode, the mode when the "
"running program is using curses.  (Its counterpart is the \"shell\" mode, "
"for when the program is not in curses.)  Subsequent calls to :func:"
"`reset_prog_mode` will restore this mode."
msgstr ""
"Guarda el modo actual del terminal como el modo \"programa\", el modo cuando "
"el programa en ejecución está utilizando curses.  (Su contrapartida es el "
"modo \"shell\", para cuando el programa no está en curses.) Las siguientes "
"llamadas a :func:`reset_prog_mode` restaurarán este modo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:153
msgid ""
"Save the current terminal mode as the \"shell\" mode, the mode when the "
"running program is not using curses.  (Its counterpart is the \"program\" "
"mode, when the program is using curses capabilities.) Subsequent calls to :"
"func:`reset_shell_mode` will restore this mode."
msgstr ""
"Guarda el modo actual del terminal como modo \"shell\", el modo cuando el "
"programa en ejecución no utiliza curses.  (Su contrapartida es el modo "
"\"programa\", cuando el programa está utilizando las capacidades de curses). "
"Las siguientes llamadas a :func:`reset_shell_mode` restaurarán este modo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:161
msgid "Insert an *ms* millisecond pause in output."
msgstr "Inserta una pausa de *ms* milisegundos en la salida."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:166
msgid ""
"Update the physical screen.  The curses library keeps two data structures, "
"one representing the current physical screen contents and a virtual screen "
"representing the desired next state.  The :func:`doupdate` function updates "
"the physical screen to match the virtual screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:171
msgid ""
"The virtual screen may be updated by a :meth:`~window.noutrefresh` call "
"after write operations such as :meth:`~window.addstr` have been performed on "
"a window.  The normal :meth:`~window.refresh` call is simply :meth:`!"
"noutrefresh` followed by :func:`!doupdate`; if you have to update multiple "
"windows, you can speed performance and perhaps reduce screen flicker by "
"issuing :meth:`!noutrefresh` calls on all windows, followed by a single :"
"func:`!doupdate`."
msgstr ""
"La pantalla virtual puede actualizarse mediante una llamada a :meth:`~window."
"noutrefresh` después de que se hayan realizado operaciones de escritura "
"como :meth:`~window.addstr` en una ventana.  La llamada normal a :meth:"
"`~window.refresh` es simplemente :meth:`!noutrefresh` seguida de :func:`!"
"doupdate`; si tiene que actualizar varias ventanas, puede acelerar el "
"rendimiento y quizás reducir el parpadeo de la pantalla realizando llamadas "
"a :meth:`!noutrefresh` en todas las ventanas, seguidas de una única :func:`!"
"doupdate`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:181
msgid ""
"Enter echo mode.  In echo mode, each character input is echoed to the screen "
"as it is entered."
msgstr ""
"Acceda al modo eco.  En el modo eco, cada carácter introducido se reproduce "
"en la pantalla a medida que se introduce."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:187
msgid "De-initialize the library, and return terminal to normal status."
msgstr "Desinicializa la biblioteca y devuelve el terminal al estado normal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:192
msgid ""
"Return the user's current erase character as a one-byte bytes object.  Under "
"Unix operating systems this is a property of the controlling tty of the "
"curses program, and is not set by the curses library itself."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el carácter de borrado actual del usuario como un objeto bytes de "
"un byte.  En sistemas operativos Unix esta es una propiedad del tty "
"controlador del programa curses, y no es establecida por la propia "
"biblioteca curses."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:199
msgid ""
"The :func:`.filter` routine, if used, must be called before :func:`initscr` "
"is called.  The effect is that, during the initialization, :envvar:`LINES` "
"is set to ``1``; the capabilities ``clear``, ``cup``, ``cud``, ``cud1``, "
"``cuu1``, ``cuu``, ``vpa`` are disabled; and the ``home`` string is set to "
"the value of ``cr``. The effect is that the cursor is confined to the "
"current line, and so are screen updates.  This may be used for enabling "
"character-at-a-time  line editing without touching the rest of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:209
msgid ""
"Flash the screen.  That is, change it to reverse-video and then change it "
"back in a short interval.  Some people prefer such as 'visible bell' to the "
"audible attention signal produced by :func:`beep`."
msgstr ""
"Haz parpadear la pantalla.  Es decir, cambiarla a vídeo inverso y luego "
"volver a cambiarla en un breve intervalo.  Algunas personas prefieren este "
"tipo de \"timbre visible\" a la señal de atención audible que produce :func:"
"`beep`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:216
msgid ""
"Flush all input buffers.  This throws away any  typeahead  that  has been "
"typed by the user and has not yet been processed by the program."
msgstr ""
"Vacía todos los búferes de entrada.  Esto desecha cualquier entrada de tipo "
"que haya sido tecleada por el usuario y que aún no haya sido procesada por "
"el programa."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:222
msgid ""
"After :meth:`~window.getch` returns :const:`KEY_MOUSE` to signal a mouse "
"event, this method should be called to retrieve the queued mouse event, "
"represented as a 5-tuple ``(id, x, y, z, bstate)``. *id* is an ID value used "
"to distinguish multiple devices, and *x*, *y*, *z* are the event's "
"coordinates.  (*z* is currently unused.)  *bstate* is an integer value whose "
"bits will be set to indicate the type of event, and will be the bitwise OR "
"of one or more of the following constants, where *n* is the button number "
"from 1 to 5: :const:`BUTTONn_PRESSED`, :const:`BUTTONn_RELEASED`, :const:"
"`BUTTONn_CLICKED`, :const:`BUTTONn_DOUBLE_CLICKED`, :const:"
"`BUTTONn_TRIPLE_CLICKED`, :const:`BUTTON_SHIFT`, :const:`BUTTON_CTRL`, :"
"const:`BUTTON_ALT`."
msgstr ""
"Después de que :meth:`~window.getch` devuelva :const:`KEY_MOUSE` para "
"señalar un evento de ratón, se debe llamar a este método para recuperar el "
"evento de ratón en cola, representado como una 5-tupla ``(id, x, y, z, "
"bstate)``. *id* es un valor ID utilizado para distinguir varios "
"dispositivos, y *x*, *y*, *z* son las coordenadas del evento.  (*z* no se "
"utiliza actualmente.) *bstate* es un valor entero cuyos bits se establecerán "
"para indicar el tipo de evento, y será el OR a nivel de bits de una o más de "
"las siguientes constantes, donde *n* es el número de botón de 1 a 5: :const:"
"`BUTTONn_PRESSED`, :const:`BUTTONn_RELEASED`, :const:`BUTTONn_CLICKED`, :"
"const:`BUTTONn_DOUBLE_CLICKED`, :const:`BUTTONn_TRIPLE_CLICKED`, :const:"
"`BUTTON_SHIFT`, :const:`BUTTON_CTRL`, :const:`BUTTON_ALT`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:233 ../../library/curses.rst:1844
msgid ""
"The ``BUTTON5_*`` constants are now exposed if they are provided by the "
"underlying curses library."
msgstr ""
"Las constantes ``BUTTON5_*`` están ahora expuestas si son proporcionadas por "
"la biblioteca curses subyacente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:240
msgid ""
"Return the current coordinates of the virtual screen cursor as a tuple ``(y, "
"x)``.  If :meth:`leaveok <window.leaveok>` is currently ``True``, then "
"return ``(-1, -1)``."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve las coordenadas actuales del cursor de la pantalla virtual como una "
"tupla ``(y, x)``.  Si :meth:`leaveok <window.leaveok>` es actualmente "
"``True``, entonces devuelve ``(-1, -1)``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:246
msgid ""
"Read window-related data stored in the file by an earlier :meth:`window."
"putwin` call. The routine then creates and initializes a new window using "
"that data, returning the new window object.  The *file* argument must be a "
"file object opened for reading in binary mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:254
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the terminal can display colors; otherwise, return "
"``False``."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si el terminal puede mostrar colores; en caso contrario, "
"devuelve ``False``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:258
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the module supports extended colors; otherwise, return "
"``False``. Extended color support allows more than 256 color pairs for "
"terminals that support more than 16 colors (for example, xterm-256color)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:262
msgid "Extended color support requires ncurses version 6.1 or later."
msgstr ""
"El soporte de color extendido requiere ncurses versión 6.1 o posterior."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:268
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the terminal has insert- and delete-character "
"capabilities. This function is included for historical reasons only, as all "
"modern software terminal emulators have such capabilities."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si el terminal tiene capacidades de inserción y borrado de "
"caracteres. Esta función se incluye sólo por razones históricas, ya que "
"todos los emuladores de terminal de software modernos tienen estas "
"capacidades."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:275
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the terminal has insert- and delete-line capabilities, or "
"can simulate  them  using scrolling regions. This function is included for "
"historical reasons only, as all modern software terminal emulators have such "
"capabilities."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si el terminal tiene capacidades de inserción y borrado de "
"líneas, o puede simularlas utilizando regiones de desplazamiento. Esta "
"función se incluye sólo por razones históricas, ya que todos los emuladores "
"de terminal de software modernos tienen tales capacidades."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:283
msgid ""
"Take a key value *ch*, and return ``True`` if the current terminal type "
"recognizes a key with that value."
msgstr ""
"Toma un valor de clave *ch*, y devuelve ``True`` si el tipo de terminal "
"actual reconoce una clave con ese valor."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:289
msgid ""
"Used for half-delay mode, which is similar to cbreak mode in that characters "
"typed by the user are immediately available to the program. However, after "
"blocking for *tenths* tenths of seconds, raise an exception if nothing has "
"been typed.  The value of *tenths* must be a number between ``1`` and "
"``255``.  Use :func:`nocbreak` to leave half-delay mode."
msgstr ""
"Usado para el modo de medio retardo, que es similar al modo cbreak en que "
"los caracteres tecleados por el usuario están inmediatamente disponibles "
"para el programa. Sin embargo, después de bloquear durante *décimas* décimas "
"de segundo, lanza una excepción si no se ha tecleado nada.  El valor de "
"*décimas* debe ser un número entre ``1`` y ``255``.  Utilice :func:"
"`nocbreak` para salir del modo de medio retardo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:298
msgid ""
"Change the definition of a color, taking the number of the color to be "
"changed followed by three RGB values (for the amounts of red, green, and "
"blue components).  The value of *color_number* must be between ``0`` and "
"``COLORS - 1``.  Each of *r*, *g*, *b*, must be a value between ``0`` and "
"``1000``.  When :func:`init_color` is used, all occurrences of that color on "
"the screen immediately change to the new definition.  This function is a no-"
"op on most terminals; it is active only if :func:`can_change_color` returns "
"``True``."
msgstr ""
"Cambia la definición de un color, tomando el número del color a cambiar "
"seguido de tres valores RGB (para las cantidades de componentes rojo, verde "
"y azul).  El valor de *número_color* debe estar comprendido entre ``0`` y "
"``COLORS - 1``.  Cada uno de *r*, *g*, *b*, debe ser un valor entre ``0`` y "
"``1000``.  Cuando se utiliza :func:`init_color`, todas las apariciones de "
"ese color en la pantalla cambian inmediatamente a la nueva definición.  Esta "
"función no funciona en la mayoría de los terminales; sólo se activa si :func:"
"`can_change_color` devuelve ``True``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:309
msgid ""
"Change the definition of a color-pair.  It takes three arguments: the number "
"of the color-pair to be changed, the foreground color number, and the "
"background color number.  The value of *pair_number* must be between ``1`` "
"and ``COLOR_PAIRS - 1`` (the ``0`` color pair can only be changed by :func:"
"`use_default_colors` and :func:`assume_default_colors`). The value of *fg* "
"and *bg* arguments must be between ``0`` and ``COLORS - 1``, or, after "
"calling :func:`!use_default_colors` or :func:`!assume_default_colors`, "
"``-1``. If the color-pair was previously initialized, the screen is "
"refreshed and all occurrences of that color-pair are changed to the new "
"definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:324
msgid ""
"Initialize the library. Return a :ref:`window <curses-window-objects>` "
"object which represents the whole screen."
msgstr ""
"Inicializa la librería. Devuelve un objeto :ref:`window <curses-window-"
"objects>` que representa toda la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:329
msgid ""
"If there is an error opening the terminal, the underlying curses library may "
"cause the interpreter to exit."
msgstr ""
"Si se produce un error al abrir el terminal, la biblioteca curses subyacente "
"puede provocar la salida del intérprete."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:335
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, pressing an interrupt key (interrupt, break, or quit) "
"will flush all output in the terminal driver queue.  If *flag* is ``False``, "
"no flushing is done."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:342
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if :func:`resize_term` would modify the window structure, "
"``False`` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si :func:`resize_term` modificaría la estructura de la "
"ventana, ``False`` en caso contrario."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:348
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if :func:`endwin` has been called (that is, the  curses "
"library has been deinitialized)."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si se ha llamado a :func:`endwin` (es decir, si se ha "
"desinicializado la biblioteca curses)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:354
msgid ""
"Return the name of the key numbered *k* as a bytes object.  The name of a "
"key generating printable ASCII character is the key's character.  The name "
"of a control-key combination is a two-byte bytes object consisting of a "
"caret (``b'^'``) followed by the corresponding printable ASCII character.  "
"The name of an alt-key combination (128--255) is a bytes object consisting "
"of the prefix ``b'M-'`` followed by the name of the corresponding ASCII "
"character."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el nombre de la clave numerada *k* como un objeto bytes.  El nombre "
"de una tecla que genera un carácter ASCII imprimible es el carácter de la "
"tecla.  El nombre de una combinación de teclas de control es un objeto bytes "
"de dos bytes formado por un signo de intercalación (``b'^'``) seguido del "
"carácter ASCII imprimible correspondiente.  El nombre de una combinación de "
"teclas alt (128--255) es un objeto de bytes formado por el prefijo ``b'M-'`` "
"seguido del nombre del carácter ASCII correspondiente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:361
msgid "Raise a :exc:`ValueError` if *k* is negative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:366
msgid ""
"Return the user's current line kill character as a one-byte bytes object. "
"Under Unix operating systems this is a property of the controlling tty of "
"the curses program, and is not set by the curses library itself."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el carácter de fin de línea actual del usuario como un objeto bytes "
"de un byte. En sistemas operativos Unix esta es una propiedad del tty "
"controlador del programa curses, y no es establecida por la propia "
"biblioteca curses."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:373
msgid ""
"Return a bytes object containing the terminfo long name field describing the "
"current terminal.  The maximum length of a verbose description is 128 "
"characters.  It is defined only after the call to :func:`initscr`."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve un objeto bytes que contiene el campo terminfo long name que "
"describe el terminal actual.  La longitud máxima de una descripción verbose "
"es de 128 caracteres.  Se define sólo después de la llamada a :func:"
"`initscr`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:380
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, allow 8-bit characters to be input.  If *flag* is "
"``False``,  allow only 7-bit chars."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``True``, permite la entrada de caracteres de 8 bits.  Si "
"*flag* es ``False``, permite sólo caracteres de 7 bits."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:386
msgid ""
"Set the maximum time in milliseconds that can elapse between press and "
"release events in order for them to be recognized as a click, and return the "
"previous interval value.  The default value is 166 milliseconds, or one "
"sixth of a second. Use a negative *interval* to obtain the interval value "
"without changing it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:394
msgid ""
"Set the mouse events to be reported, and return a tuple ``(availmask, "
"oldmask)``.   *availmask* indicates which of the specified mouse events can "
"be reported; on complete failure it returns ``0``.  *oldmask* is the "
"previous value of the mouse event mask.  If this function is never called, "
"no mouse events are ever reported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:403
msgid "Sleep for *ms* milliseconds."
msgstr "Dormir durante *ms* milisegundos."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:408
msgid ""
"Create and return a pointer to a new pad data structure with the given "
"number of lines and columns.  Return a pad as a window object."
msgstr ""
"Crea y devuelve un puntero a una nueva estructura de datos de pad con el "
"número dado de líneas y columnas.  Devuelve un pad como objeto ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:411
msgid ""
"A pad is like a window, except that it is not restricted by the screen size, "
"and is not necessarily associated with a particular part of the screen.  "
"Pads can be used when a large window is needed, and only a part of the "
"window will be on the screen at one time.  Automatic refreshes of pads (such "
"as from scrolling or echoing of input) do not occur.  The :meth:`~window."
"refresh` and :meth:`~window.noutrefresh` methods of a pad require 6 "
"arguments to specify the part of the pad to be displayed and the location on "
"the screen to be used for the display. The arguments are *pminrow*, "
"*pmincol*, *sminrow*, *smincol*, *smaxrow*, *smaxcol*; the *p* arguments "
"refer to the upper-left corner of the pad region to be displayed and the *s* "
"arguments define a clipping box on the screen within which the pad region is "
"to be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:427
msgid ""
"Return a new :ref:`window <curses-window-objects>`, whose left-upper corner "
"is at  ``(begin_y, begin_x)``, and whose height/width is  *nlines*/*ncols*."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve una nueva :ref:`window <curses-window-objects>`, cuya esquina "
"superior izquierda está en ``(begin_y, begin_x)``, y cuya altura/anchura es "
"*nlines*/*ncols*."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:430
msgid ""
"By default, the window will extend from the  specified position to the lower "
"right corner of the screen."
msgstr ""
"Por defecto, la ventana se extenderá desde la posición especificada hasta la "
"esquina inferior derecha de la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:436
msgid ""
"Enter newline mode.  This mode translates the return key into newline on "
"input, and translates newline into return and line-feed on output. Newline "
"mode is initially on."
msgstr ""
"Entra en el modo nueva línea.  Este modo convierte la tecla de retorno en "
"nueva línea en la entrada, y convierte la nueva línea en retorno y salto de "
"línea en la salida. El modo nueva línea está activado inicialmente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:440
msgid "If *flag* is ``False``, the effect is the same as calling :func:`nonl`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:445
msgid ""
"Leave cbreak mode.  Return to normal \"cooked\" mode with line buffering."
msgstr ""
"Salir del modo cbreak.  Vuelve al modo normal \"cooked\" con búfer de línea."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:450
msgid "Leave echo mode.  Echoing of input characters is turned off."
msgstr ""
"Salir del modo eco.  Se desactiva el eco de los caracteres introducidos."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:455
msgid ""
"Leave newline mode.  Disable translation of return into newline on input, "
"and disable low-level translation of newline into newline/return on output "
"(but this does not change the behavior of ``addch('\\n')``, which always "
"does the equivalent of return and line feed on the virtual screen).  With "
"translation off, curses can sometimes speed up vertical motion a little; "
"also, it will be able to detect the return key on input."
msgstr ""
"Dejar el modo de nueva línea.  Desactivar la traducción de retorno a nueva "
"línea en la entrada, y desactivar la traducción de bajo nivel de nueva línea "
"a nueva línea/retorno en la salida (pero esto no cambia el comportamiento de "
"``addch('\\n')``, que siempre hace el equivalente de retorno y salto de "
"línea en la pantalla virtual).  Con la traducción desactivada, curses puede "
"a veces acelerar un poco el movimiento vertical; además, será capaz de "
"detectar la tecla return en la entrada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:465
msgid ""
"When the :func:`!noqiflush` routine is used, normal flush of input and "
"output queues associated with the ``INTR``, ``QUIT`` and ``SUSP`` characters "
"will not be done.  You may want to call :func:`!noqiflush` in a signal "
"handler if you want output to continue as though the interrupt had not "
"occurred, after the handler exits."
msgstr ""
"Cuando se utiliza la rutina :func:`!noqiflush`, no se realiza el vaciado "
"normal de las colas de entrada y salida asociadas a los caracteres ``INTR``, "
"``QUIT`` y ``SUSP``.  Es posible que desee llamar a :func:`!noqiflush` en un "
"manejador de señales si desea que la salida continúe como si la interrupción "
"no se hubiera producido, después de que el manejador salga."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:473
msgid "Leave raw mode. Return to normal \"cooked\" mode with line buffering."
msgstr ""
"Salir del modo raw. Volver al modo normal \"cooked\" con búfer de línea."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:478
msgid ""
"Return a tuple ``(fg, bg)`` containing the colors for the requested color "
"pair. The value of *pair_number* must be between ``0`` and ``COLOR_PAIRS - "
"1``."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve una tupla ``(fg, bg)`` que contiene los colores del par de colores "
"solicitado. El valor de *pair_number* debe estar comprendido entre ``0`` y "
"``COLOR_PAIRS - 1``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:484
msgid ""
"Return the number of the color-pair set by the attribute value *attr*. :func:"
"`color_pair` is the counterpart to this function."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el número del par de colores establecido por el valor del atributo "
"*attr*. :func:`color_pair` es la contrapartida de esta función."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:490
msgid ""
"Equivalent to ``tputs(str, 1, putchar)``; emit the value of a specified "
"terminfo capability for the current terminal.  Note that the output of :func:"
"`putp` always goes to standard output."
msgstr ""
"Equivale a ``tputs(str, 1, putchar)``; emite el valor de una capacidad "
"terminfo especificada para el terminal actual.  Tenga en cuenta que la "
"salida de :func:`putp` siempre va a la salida estándar."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:494 ../../library/curses.rst:630
#: ../../library/curses.rst:640 ../../library/curses.rst:650
#: ../../library/curses.rst:660
msgid ":func:`setupterm` (or :func:`initscr`) must be called first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:499
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``False``, the effect is the same as calling :func:`noqiflush`. "
"If *flag* is ``True``, or no argument is provided, the queues will be "
"flushed when these control characters are read."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``False``, el efecto es el mismo que llamar a :func:"
"`noqiflush`. Si *flag* es ``True``, o no se proporciona ningún argumento, "
"las colas se vaciarán cuando se lean estos caracteres de control."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:506
msgid ""
"Enter raw mode.  In raw mode, normal line buffering and  processing of "
"interrupt, quit, suspend, and flow control keys are turned off; characters "
"are presented to curses input functions one by one."
msgstr ""
"Entrar en modo raw.  En el modo raw, el almacenamiento en búfer de la línea "
"normal y el procesamiento de las teclas de interrupción, salida, suspensión "
"y control de flujo están desactivados; los caracteres se presentan a las "
"funciones de entrada curses uno a uno."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:513
msgid ""
"Restore the  terminal  to \"program\" mode, as previously saved  by :func:"
"`def_prog_mode`."
msgstr ""
"Restablecer el terminal al modo \"program\", tal y como se guardó "
"anteriormente mediante :func:`def_prog_mode`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:519
msgid ""
"Restore the  terminal  to \"shell\" mode, as previously saved  by :func:"
"`def_shell_mode`."
msgstr ""
"Restaura el terminal al modo \"shell\", tal y como se guardó previamente en :"
"func:`def_shell_mode`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:525
msgid ""
"Restore the state of the terminal modes to what it was at the last call to :"
"func:`savetty`."
msgstr ""
"Restaura el estado de los modos del terminal al que tenían en la última "
"llamada a :func:`savetty`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:531
msgid ""
"Backend function used by :func:`resizeterm`, performing most of the work; "
"when resizing the windows, :func:`resize_term` blank-fills the areas that "
"are extended.  The calling application should fill in these areas with "
"appropriate data.  The :func:`!resize_term` function attempts to resize all "
"windows.  However, due to the calling convention of pads, it is not possible "
"to resize these without additional interaction with the application."
msgstr ""
"Función backend utilizada por :func:`resizeterm`, que realiza la mayor parte "
"del trabajo; al redimensionar las ventanas, :func:`resize_term` rellena en "
"blanco las áreas que se amplían.  La aplicación que llama debe rellenar "
"estas áreas con los datos apropiados.  La función :func:`!resize_term` "
"intenta redimensionar todas las ventanas.  Sin embargo, debido a la "
"convención de llamada de los pads, no es posible redimensionarlas sin una "
"interacción adicional con la aplicación."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:541
msgid ""
"Resize the standard and current windows to the specified dimensions, and "
"adjusts other bookkeeping data used by the curses library that record the "
"window dimensions (in particular the SIGWINCH handler)."
msgstr ""
"Redimensiona las ventanas estándar y actual a las dimensiones especificadas, "
"y ajusta otros datos de contabilidad utilizados por la biblioteca curses que "
"registran las dimensiones de la ventana (en particular el manejador "
"SIGWINCH)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:548
msgid ""
"Save the current state of the terminal modes in a buffer, usable by :func:"
"`resetty`."
msgstr ""
"Guarda el estado actual de los modos del terminal en un buffer, utilizable "
"por :func:`resetty`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:553
msgid "Retrieves the value set by :func:`set_escdelay`."
msgstr "Recupera el valor establecido por :func:`set_escdelay`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:559
msgid ""
"Sets the number of milliseconds to wait after reading an escape character, "
"to distinguish between an individual escape character entered on the "
"keyboard from escape sequences sent by cursor and function keys."
msgstr ""
"Establece el número de milisegundos a esperar después de leer un carácter de "
"escape, para distinguir entre un carácter de escape individual introducido "
"en el teclado de las secuencias de escape enviadas por el cursor y las "
"teclas de función."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:567
msgid "Retrieves the value set by :func:`set_tabsize`."
msgstr "Recupera el valor establecido por :func:`set_tabsize`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:573
msgid ""
"Sets the number of columns used by the curses library when converting a tab "
"character to spaces as it adds the tab to a window."
msgstr ""
"Establece el número de columnas utilizadas por la biblioteca curses cuando "
"convierte un carácter de tabulación en espacios al añadir la tabulación a "
"una ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:580
msgid ""
"Set the virtual screen cursor to *y*, *x*. If *y* and *x* are both ``-1``, "
"then :meth:`leaveok <window.leaveok>` is set ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Establece el cursor de la pantalla virtual en *y*, *x*. Si *y* y *x* son "
"ambos ``-1``, entonces :meth:`leaveok <window.leaveok>` se establece "
"``True``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:586
msgid ""
"Initialize the terminal.  *term* is a string giving the terminal name, or "
"``None``; if omitted or ``None``, the value of the :envvar:`TERM` "
"environment variable will be used.  *fd* is the file descriptor to which any "
"initialization sequences will be sent; if not supplied or ``-1``, the file "
"descriptor for ``sys.stdout`` will be used."
msgstr ""
"Inicializar el terminal.  *term* es una cadena que indica el nombre del "
"terminal, o ``None``; si se omite o ``None``, se utilizará el valor de la "
"variable de entorno :envvar:`TERM`.  *fd* es el descriptor de fichero al que "
"se enviará cualquier secuencia de inicialización; si no se proporciona o "
"``-1``, se utilizará el descriptor de fichero para ``sys.stdout``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:592
msgid ""
"Raise a :exc:`curses.error` if the terminal could not be found or its "
"terminfo database entry could not be read.  If the terminal has already been "
"initialized, this function has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:599
msgid ""
"Must be called if the programmer wants to use colors, and before any other "
"color manipulation routine is called.  It is good practice to call this "
"routine right after :func:`initscr`."
msgstr ""
"Debe llamarse si el programador desea utilizar colores, y antes de llamar a "
"cualquier otra rutina de manipulación de colores.  Es una buena práctica "
"llamar a esta rutina justo después de :func:`initscr`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:603
msgid ""
":func:`start_color` initializes eight basic colors (black, red,  green, "
"yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, and white), and two global variables in the :"
"mod:`!curses` module, :const:`COLORS` and :const:`COLOR_PAIRS`, containing "
"the maximum number of colors and color-pairs the terminal can support.  It "
"also restores the colors on the terminal to the values they had when the "
"terminal was just turned on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:612
msgid ""
"Return a logical OR of all video attributes supported by the terminal.  This "
"information is useful when a curses program needs complete control over the "
"appearance of the screen."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve un OR lógico de todos los atributos de vídeo soportados por el "
"terminal.  Esta información es útil cuando un programa curses necesita un "
"control total sobre la apariencia de la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:619
msgid ""
"Return the value of the environment variable :envvar:`TERM`, as a bytes "
"object, truncated to 14 characters."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el valor de la variable de entorno :envvar:`TERM`, como un objeto "
"bytes, truncado a 14 caracteres."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:625
msgid ""
"Return the value of the Boolean capability corresponding to the terminfo "
"capability name *capname* as an integer.  Return the value ``-1`` if "
"*capname* is not a Boolean capability, or ``0`` if it is canceled or absent "
"from the terminal description."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el valor de la capacidad booleana correspondiente al nombre de "
"capacidad terminfo *capname* como un entero.  Devuelve el valor ``-1`` si "
"*capname* no es una capacidad booleana, o ``0`` si está cancelada o ausente "
"en la descripción del terminal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:635
msgid ""
"Return the value of the numeric capability corresponding to the terminfo "
"capability name *capname* as an integer.  Return the value ``-2`` if "
"*capname* is not a numeric capability, or ``-1`` if it is canceled or absent "
"from the terminal description."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el valor de la capacidad numérica correspondiente al nombre de "
"capacidad terminfo *capname* como un entero.  Devuelve el valor ``-2`` si "
"*capname* no es una capacidad numérica, o ``-1`` si está cancelada o ausente "
"en la descripción del terminal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:645
msgid ""
"Return the value of the string capability corresponding to the terminfo "
"capability name *capname* as a bytes object.  Return ``None`` if *capname* "
"is not a terminfo \"string capability\", or is canceled or absent from the "
"terminal description."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el valor de la capacidad de cadena correspondiente al nombre de "
"capacidad terminfo *capname* como un objeto bytes.  Devuelve ``None`` si "
"*capname* no es una \"capacidad de cadena\" terminfo, o está cancelada o "
"ausente de la descripción del terminal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:655
msgid ""
"Instantiate the bytes object *str* with the supplied parameters, where *str* "
"should be a parameterized string obtained from the terminfo database.  For "
"example, ``tparm(tigetstr(\"cup\"), 5, 3)`` could result in "
"``b'\\033[6;4H'``, the exact result depending on terminal type.  Up to nine "
"integer parameters may be supplied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:665
msgid ""
"Specify that the file descriptor *fd* be used for typeahead checking.  If "
"*fd* is ``-1``, then no typeahead checking is done."
msgstr ""
"Especifica que se utilice el descriptor de fichero *fd* para la comprobación "
"de tipo.  Si *fd* es ``-1``, no se realiza ninguna comprobación de tipo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:668
msgid ""
"The curses library does \"line-breakout optimization\" by looking for "
"typeahead periodically while updating the screen.  If input is found, and it "
"is coming from a tty, the current update is postponed until refresh or "
"doupdate is called again, allowing faster response to commands typed in "
"advance. This function allows specifying a different file descriptor for "
"typeahead checking."
msgstr ""
"La biblioteca curses hace una \"optimización de salto de línea\" buscando "
"typeahead periódicamente mientras actualiza la pantalla.  Si la entrada es "
"encontrada, y viene de un tty, la actualización actual es pospuesta hasta "
"que refresh o doupdate es llamado de nuevo, permitiendo una respuesta más "
"rápida a los comandos tecleados por adelantado. Esta función permite "
"especificar un descriptor de fichero diferente para la comprobación "
"typeahead."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:677
msgid ""
"Return a bytes object which is a printable representation of the character "
"*ch*. Control characters are represented as a caret followed by the "
"character, for example as ``b'^C'``. Printing characters are left as they "
"are."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve un objeto bytes que es una representación imprimible del carácter "
"*ch*. Los caracteres de control se representan como un signo de "
"intercalación seguido del carácter, por ejemplo ``b'^C'``. Los caracteres de "
"impresión se dejan tal cual."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:684
msgid "Push *ch* so the next :meth:`~window.getch` will return it."
msgstr "Pulsa *ch* para que el siguiente :meth:`~window.getch` lo devuelva."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:688
msgid "Only one *ch* can be pushed before :meth:`!getch` is called."
msgstr "Sólo se puede pulsar una *ch* antes de llamar a :meth:`!getch`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:693
msgid ""
"Update the :const:`LINES` and :const:`COLS` module variables. Useful for "
"detecting manual screen resize."
msgstr ""
"Actualiza las variables de los módulos :const:`LINES` y :const:`COLS`. Útil "
"para detectar el redimensionamiento manual de la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:701
msgid "Push *ch* so the next :meth:`~window.get_wch` will return it."
msgstr "Pulsa *ch* para que el siguiente :meth:`~window.get_wch` lo devuelva."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:705
msgid "Only one *ch* can be pushed before :meth:`!get_wch` is called."
msgstr "Sólo se puede pulsar una *ch* antes de llamar a :meth:`!get_wch`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:712
msgid ""
"Push a :const:`KEY_MOUSE` event onto the input queue, associating the given "
"state data with it."
msgstr ""
"Coloca un evento :const:`KEY_MOUSE` en la cola de entrada, asociándole los "
"datos de estado dados."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:718
msgid ""
"If used, this function should be called before :func:`initscr` or newterm "
"are called.  When *flag* is ``False``, the values of lines and columns "
"specified in the terminfo database will be used, even if environment "
"variables :envvar:`LINES` and :envvar:`COLUMNS` (used by default) are set, "
"or if curses is running in a window (in which case default behavior would be "
"to use the window size if :envvar:`LINES` and :envvar:`COLUMNS` are not set)."
msgstr ""
"Si se usa, se debe llamar esta función antes de que se llamen:func:`initscr` "
"o newterm.  Cuando *flag* es ``False``, se usarán los valores de líneas y "
"columnas especificados en la base de datos terminfo, incluso si las "
"variables de entorno :envvar:`LINES` y :envvar:`COLUMNS` (usadas por "
"defecto) están establecidas, o si curses se está ejecutando en una ventana "
"(en cuyo caso el comportamiento por defecto sería usar el tamaño de la "
"ventana si :envvar:`LINES` y :envvar:`COLUMNS` no están establecidas)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:728
msgid "Equivalent to ``assume_default_colors(-1, -1)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:733
msgid ""
"Initialize curses and call another callable object, *func*, which should be "
"the rest of your curses-using application.  If the application raises an "
"exception, this function will restore the terminal to a sane state before re-"
"raising the exception and generating a traceback.  The callable object "
"*func* is then passed the main window 'stdscr' as its first argument, "
"followed by any other arguments passed to :func:`!wrapper`.  Before calling "
"*func*, :func:`!wrapper` turns on cbreak mode, turns off echo, enables the "
"terminal keypad, and initializes colors if the terminal has color support.  "
"On exit (whether normally or by exception) it restores cooked mode, turns on "
"echo, and disables the terminal keypad."
msgstr ""
"Inicializa curses y llama a otro objeto invocable, *func*, que debería ser "
"el resto de la aplicación que utiliza curses.  Si la aplicación lanza una "
"excepción, esta función restaurará el terminal a un estado sano antes de "
"volver a lanzar la excepción y generar un rastreo.  Al objeto invocable "
"*func* se le pasa la ventana principal 'stdscr' como primer argumento, "
"seguido de cualquier otro argumento pasado a :func:`!wrapper`. Antes de "
"llamar a *func*, :func:`!wrapper` activa el modo cbreak, desactiva echo, "
"activa el teclado del terminal, e inicializa los colores si el terminal "
"tiene soporte de color.  Al salir (normalmente o por excepción), restaura el "
"modo cocinado, activa el eco y desactiva el teclado del terminal."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:747
msgid "Window objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:751
msgid ""
"Window objects, as returned by :func:`initscr` and :func:`newwin` above, "
"have the following methods and attributes:"
msgstr ""
"Los objetos Window, devueltos por :func:`initscr` y :func:`newwin`, tienen "
"los siguientes métodos y atributos:"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:758
msgid ""
"Paint character *ch* at ``(y, x)`` with attributes *attr*, overwriting any "
"character previously painted at that location.  By default, the character "
"position and attributes are the current settings for the window object."
msgstr ""
"Pinta el carácter *ch* en ``(y, x)`` con los atributos *attr*, "
"sobrescribiendo cualquier carácter pintado previamente en esa ubicación.  "
"Por defecto, la posición del carácter y los atributos son los ajustes "
"actuales para el objeto ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:764
msgid ""
"Writing outside the window, subwindow, or pad raises a :exc:`curses.error`. "
"Attempting to write to the lower-right corner of a window, subwindow, or pad "
"will cause an exception to be raised after the character is printed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:772
msgid ""
"Paint at most *n* characters of the character string *str* at ``(y, x)`` "
"with attributes *attr*, overwriting anything previously on the display."
msgstr ""
"Pinta como máximo *n* caracteres de la cadena de caracteres *str* en ``(y, "
"x)`` con los atributos *attr*, sobrescribiendo todo lo que había previamente "
"en la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:780
msgid ""
"Paint the character string *str* at ``(y, x)`` with attributes *attr*, "
"overwriting anything previously on the display."
msgstr ""
"Pinta la cadena de caracteres *str* en ``(y, x)`` con los atributos *attr*, "
"sobrescribiendo todo lo que había previamente en la pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:785
msgid ""
"Writing outside the window, subwindow, or pad raises :exc:`curses.error`. "
"Attempting to write to the lower-right corner of a window, subwindow, or pad "
"will cause an exception to be raised after the string is printed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:789
msgid ""
"A bug in ncurses, the backend for this Python module, could cause segfaults "
"when resizing windows.  This was fixed in ncurses-6.1-20190511. If you are "
"stuck with an earlier ncurses, you can avoid triggering it by not calling :"
"meth:`!addstr` with a *str* that has embedded newlines; instead, call :meth:"
"`!addstr` separately for each line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:798
msgid ""
"Remove attribute *attr* from the \"background\" set applied to all writes to "
"the current window."
msgstr ""
"Elimina el atributo *attr* del conjunto \"background\" aplicado a todas las "
"escrituras en la ventana actual."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:804
msgid ""
"Add attribute *attr* to the \"background\" set applied to all writes to the "
"current window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:810
msgid ""
"Set the \"background\" set of attributes to *attr*.  This set is initially "
"``0`` (no attributes)."
msgstr ""
"Establece el conjunto de atributos \"background\" en *attr*.  Este conjunto "
"es inicialmente ``0`` (sin atributos)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:816
msgid ""
"Set the background property of the window to the character *ch*, with "
"attributes *attr*.  The change is then applied to every character position "
"in that window:"
msgstr ""
"Establece la propiedad background de la ventana al carácter *ch*, con "
"atributos *attr*.  El cambio se aplica entonces a cada posición de carácter "
"en esa ventana:"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:820
msgid ""
"The attribute of every character in the window  is changed to the new "
"background attribute."
msgstr ""
"El atributo de cada carácter de la ventana se cambia al nuevo atributo de "
"fondo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:823
msgid ""
"Wherever  the  former background character appears, it is changed to the new "
"background character."
msgstr ""
"Dondequiera que aparezca el antiguo personaje de fondo, se cambia por el "
"nuevo personaje de fondo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:829
msgid ""
"Set the window's background.  A window's background consists of a character "
"and any combination of attributes.  The attribute part of the background is "
"combined (OR'ed) with all non-blank characters that are written into the "
"window.  Both the character and attribute parts of the background are "
"combined with the blank characters.  The background becomes a property of "
"the character and moves with the character through any scrolling and insert/"
"delete line/character operations."
msgstr ""
"Establece el fondo de la ventana.  El fondo de una ventana consiste en un "
"carácter y cualquier combinación de atributos.  La parte de atributos del "
"fondo se combina (OR'ed) con todos los caracteres no vacíos que se escriben "
"en la ventana.  Tanto la parte de carácter como la parte de atributo del "
"fondo se combinan con los caracteres en blanco.  El fondo se convierte en "
"una propiedad del carácter y se desplaza con él a través de las operaciones "
"de desplazamiento e inserción/eliminación de líneas/caracteres."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:839
msgid ""
"Draw a border around the edges of the window. Each parameter specifies  the "
"character to use for a specific part of the border; see the table below for "
"more details."
msgstr ""
"Dibuja un borde alrededor de los bordes de la ventana. Cada parámetro "
"especifica el carácter a utilizar para una parte específica del borde; véase "
"la tabla siguiente para más detalles."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:845
msgid ""
"A ``0`` value for any parameter will cause the default character to be used "
"for that parameter.  Keyword parameters can *not* be used.  The defaults are "
"listed in this table:"
msgstr ""
"Un valor ``0`` para cualquier parámetro hará que se utilice el carácter por "
"defecto para ese parámetro.  Los parámetros de palabra clave *no* pueden "
"utilizarse.  Los valores por defecto se enumeran en esta tabla:"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:850
msgid "Parameter"
msgstr "Parámetro"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:850
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Description"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:850
msgid "Default value"
msgstr "Valor por defecto"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:852
msgid "*ls*"
msgstr "*ls*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:852
msgid "Left side"
msgstr "Lado izquierdo"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:852 ../../library/curses.rst:854
msgid ":const:`ACS_VLINE`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_VLINE`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:854
msgid "*rs*"
msgstr "*rs*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:854
msgid "Right side"
msgstr "Lado derecho"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:856
msgid "*ts*"
msgstr "*ts*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:856
msgid "Top"
msgstr "Top"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:856 ../../library/curses.rst:858
msgid ":const:`ACS_HLINE`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_HLINE`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:858
msgid "*bs*"
msgstr "*bs*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:858
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr "Fondo"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:860
msgid "*tl*"
msgstr "*tl*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:860
msgid "Upper-left corner"
msgstr "Esquina superior izquierda"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:860
msgid ":const:`ACS_ULCORNER`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_ULCORNER`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:862
msgid "*tr*"
msgstr "*tr*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:862
msgid "Upper-right corner"
msgstr "Esquina superior derecha"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:862
msgid ":const:`ACS_URCORNER`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_URCORNER`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:864
msgid "*bl*"
msgstr "*bl*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:864
msgid "Bottom-left corner"
msgstr "Esquina inferior izquierda"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:864
msgid ":const:`ACS_LLCORNER`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_LLCORNER`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:866
msgid "*br*"
msgstr "*br*"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:866
msgid "Bottom-right corner"
msgstr "Esquina inferior derecha"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:866
msgid ":const:`ACS_LRCORNER`"
msgstr ":const:`ACS_LRCORNER`"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:872
msgid ""
"Similar to :meth:`border`, but both *ls* and *rs* are *vertch* and both *ts* "
"and *bs* are *horch*.  The default corner characters are always used by this "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Similar a :meth:`border`, pero tanto *ls* como *rs* son *vertch* y tanto "
"*ts* como *bs* son *horch*.  Esta función utiliza siempre los caracteres de "
"esquina predeterminados."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:881
msgid ""
"Set the attributes of *num* characters at the current cursor position, or at "
"position ``(y, x)`` if supplied. If *num* is not given or is ``-1``, the "
"attribute will be set on all the characters to the end of the line.  This "
"function moves cursor to position ``(y, x)`` if supplied. The changed line "
"will be touched using the :meth:`touchline` method so that the contents will "
"be redisplayed by the next window refresh."
msgstr ""
"Establece los atributos de *num* caracteres en la posición actual del "
"cursor, o en la posición ``(y, x)`` si se proporciona. Si *num* no se "
"proporciona o es ``-1``, el atributo se establecerá en todos los caracteres "
"hasta el final de la línea.  Esta función mueve el cursor a la posición "
"``(y, x)`` si se proporciona. La línea modificada se tocará utilizando el "
"método :meth:`touchline` para que el contenido se vuelva a mostrar en la "
"siguiente actualización de la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:891
msgid ""
"Like :meth:`erase`, but also cause the whole window to be repainted upon "
"next call to :meth:`refresh`."
msgstr ""
"Como :meth:`erase`, pero también hace que se vuelva a pintar toda la ventana "
"en la siguiente llamada a :meth:`refresh`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:897
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, the next call to :meth:`refresh` will clear the "
"window completely."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``True``, la siguiente llamada a :meth:`refresh` borrará la "
"ventana completamente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:903
msgid ""
"Erase from cursor to the end of the window: all lines below the cursor are "
"deleted, and then the equivalent of :meth:`clrtoeol` is performed."
msgstr ""
"Borrar desde el cursor hasta el final de la ventana: se borran todas las "
"líneas por debajo del cursor y, a continuación, se realiza el equivalente "
"de :meth:`clrtoeol`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:909
msgid "Erase from cursor to the end of the line."
msgstr "Borrar desde el cursor hasta el final de la línea."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:914
msgid ""
"Update the current cursor position of all the ancestors of the window to "
"reflect the current cursor position of the window."
msgstr ""
"Actualiza la posición actual del cursor de todos los ancestros de la ventana "
"para reflejar la posición actual del cursor de la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:920
msgid ""
"Delete the character under the cursor, or at ``(y, x)`` if specified.  All "
"characters to the right on the same line are shifted one position left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:926
msgid ""
"Delete the line under the cursor. All following lines are moved up by one "
"line."
msgstr ""
"Borra la línea situada bajo el cursor. Todas las líneas siguientes se "
"desplazan una línea hacia arriba."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:932
msgid ""
"An abbreviation for \"derive window\", :meth:`derwin` is the same as "
"calling :meth:`subwin`, except that *begin_y* and *begin_x* are relative to "
"the origin of the window, rather than relative to the entire screen.  Return "
"a window object for the derived window."
msgstr ""
"Abreviatura de \"derivar ventana\", :meth:`derwin` es lo mismo que llamar a :"
"meth:`subwin`, salvo que *begin_y* y *begin_x* son relativos al origen de la "
"ventana, en lugar de relativos a toda la pantalla.  Devuelve un objeto "
"ventana para la ventana derivada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:940
msgid ""
"Add character *ch* with attribute *attr*, and immediately  call :meth:"
"`refresh` on the window."
msgstr ""
"Añade el carácter *ch* con el atributo *attr*, e inmediatamente llama a :"
"meth:`refresh` en la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:946
msgid ""
"Test whether the given pair of screen-relative character-cell coordinates "
"are enclosed by the given window, returning ``True`` or ``False``.  It is "
"useful for determining what subset of the screen windows enclose the "
"location of a mouse event."
msgstr ""
"Comprueba si el par dado de coordenadas de celda-carácter relativas a la "
"pantalla están encerradas por la ventana dada, devolviendo ``True`` o "
"``False``. Es útil para determinar qué subconjunto de ventanas de pantalla "
"encierran la ubicación de un evento de ratón."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:951
msgid "Previously it returned ``1`` or ``0`` instead of ``True`` or ``False``."
msgstr "Antes devolvía ``1`` o ``0`` en lugar de ``True`` o ``False``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:957
msgid ""
"Encoding used to encode method arguments (Unicode strings and characters). "
"The encoding attribute is inherited from the parent window when a subwindow "
"is created, for example with :meth:`window.subwin`. By default, current "
"locale encoding is used (see :func:`locale.getencoding`)."
msgstr ""
"Codificación utilizada para codificar los argumentos del método (cadenas y "
"caracteres Unicode). El atributo encoding se hereda de la ventana padre "
"cuando se crea una subventana, por ejemplo con :meth:`window.subwin`. Por "
"defecto, se utiliza la codificación de la configuración regional actual "
"(véase :func:`locale.getencoding`)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:967
msgid "Clear the window."
msgstr "Despeja la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:972
msgid "Return a tuple ``(y, x)`` of coordinates of upper-left corner."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve una tupla ``(y, x)`` de coordenadas de la esquina superior "
"izquierda."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:977
msgid "Return the given window's current background character/attribute pair."
msgstr "Devuelve el par carácter/atributo de fondo actual de la ventana dada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:982
msgid ""
"Get a character. Note that the integer returned does *not* have to be in "
"ASCII range: function keys, keypad keys and so on are represented by numbers "
"higher than 255.  In no-delay mode, return ``-1`` if there is no input, "
"otherwise wait until a key is pressed."
msgstr ""
"Obtener un carácter. Tenga en cuenta que el entero devuelto *no* tiene que "
"estar en el rango ASCII: las teclas de función, las teclas del teclado y "
"demás se representan con números superiores a 255.  En modo sin retardo, "
"devuelve ``-1`` si no hay entrada, en caso contrario espera hasta que se "
"pulse una tecla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:990
msgid ""
"Get a wide character. Return a character for most keys, or an integer for "
"function keys, keypad keys, and other special keys. In no-delay mode, raise "
"an exception if there is no input."
msgstr ""
"Obtener un carácter ancho. Devuelve un carácter para la mayoría de las "
"teclas, o un entero para las teclas de función, las teclas del teclado y "
"otras teclas especiales. En modo sin retardo, lanza una excepción si no hay "
"entrada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:999
msgid ""
"Get a character, returning a string instead of an integer, as :meth:`getch` "
"does. Function keys, keypad keys and other special keys return a multibyte "
"string containing the key name.  In no-delay mode, raise an exception if "
"there is no input."
msgstr ""
"Obtiene un carácter, devolviendo una cadena en lugar de un entero, como "
"hace :meth:`getch`. Las teclas de función, teclado y otras teclas especiales "
"devuelven una cadena multibyte que contiene el nombre de la tecla.  En modo "
"sin retardo, lanza una excepción si no hay entrada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1007
msgid "Return a tuple ``(y, x)`` of the height and width of the window."
msgstr "Devuelve una tupla ``(y, x)`` de la altura y la anchura de la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1012
msgid ""
"Return the beginning coordinates of this window relative to its parent "
"window as a tuple ``(y, x)``.  Return ``(-1, -1)`` if this window has no "
"parent."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve las coordenadas iniciales de esta ventana respecto a su ventana "
"padre como una tupla ``(y, x)``.  Devuelve ``(-1, -1)`` si esta ventana no "
"tiene padre."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1022
msgid ""
"Read a bytes object from the user, with primitive line editing capacity. At "
"most *n* characters are read; *n* defaults to and cannot exceed 2047."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1026 ../../library/curses.rst:1125
msgid "The maximum value for *n* was increased from 1023 to 2047."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1032
msgid ""
"Return a tuple ``(y, x)`` of current cursor position  relative to the "
"window's upper-left corner."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve una tupla ``(y, x)`` de la posición actual del cursor relativa a la "
"esquina superior izquierda de la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1039
msgid ""
"Display a horizontal line starting at ``(y, x)`` with length *n* consisting "
"of the character *ch* with attributes *attr*.  The line stops at the right "
"edge of the window if fewer than *n* cells are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1046
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``False``, curses no longer considers using the hardware insert/"
"delete character feature of the terminal; if *flag* is ``True``, use of "
"character insertion and deletion is enabled.  When curses is first "
"initialized, use of character insert/delete is enabled by default."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``False``, curses ya no considera el uso de la característica "
"hardware de inserción/borrado de caracteres del terminal; si *flag* es "
"``True``, se habilita el uso de inserción y borrado de caracteres.  Cuando "
"curses se inicializa por primera vez, el uso de inserción/borrado de "
"caracteres está habilitado por defecto."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1054
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, :mod:`!curses` will try to use hardware line editing "
"facilities.  Otherwise, curses will not use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1060
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, any change in the window image automatically causes "
"the window to be refreshed; you no longer have to call :meth:`refresh` "
"yourself. However, it may degrade performance considerably, due to repeated "
"calls to wrefresh.  This option is disabled by default."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``True``, cualquier cambio en la imagen de la ventana hace que "
"ésta se actualice automáticamente; ya no tiene que llamar usted mismo a :"
"meth:`refresh`. Sin embargo, puede degradar el rendimiento "
"considerablemente, debido a las repetidas llamadas a wrefresh.  Esta opción "
"está desactivada por defecto."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1068
msgid ""
"Return the character at the given position in the window. The bottom 8 bits "
"are the character proper, and upper bits are the attributes."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve el carácter en la posición dada en la ventana. Los 8 bits "
"inferiores son el carácter propiamente dicho, y los bits superiores son los "
"atributos."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1075
msgid ""
"Insert character *ch* with attributes *attr* before the character under the "
"cursor, or at ``(y, x)`` if specified.  All characters to the right of the "
"cursor are shifted one position right, with the rightmost character on the "
"line being lost.  The cursor position does not change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1083
msgid ""
"Insert *nlines* lines into the specified window above the current line.  The "
"*nlines* bottom lines are lost.  For negative *nlines*, delete *nlines* "
"lines starting with the one under the cursor, and move the remaining lines "
"up.  The bottom *nlines* lines are cleared.  The current cursor position "
"remains the same."
msgstr ""
"Inserta *nlines* líneas en la ventana especificada por encima de la línea "
"actual.  Las *nlines* inferiores se pierden.  Para *nlines* negativas, "
"borrar *nlines* líneas empezando por la que está bajo el cursor, y mover las "
"líneas restantes hacia arriba.  Las líneas *nlines* inferiores se borran.  "
"La posición actual del cursor permanece igual."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1092
msgid ""
"Insert a blank line under the cursor. All following lines are moved down by "
"one line."
msgstr ""
"Inserta una línea en blanco bajo el cursor. Todas las líneas siguientes se "
"desplazan una línea hacia abajo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1099
msgid ""
"Insert a character string (as many characters as will fit on the line) "
"before the character under the cursor, up to *n* characters.   If *n* is "
"zero or negative, the entire string is inserted. All characters to the right "
"of the cursor are shifted right, with the rightmost characters on the line "
"being lost. The cursor position does not change (after moving to *y*, *x*, "
"if specified)."
msgstr ""
"Inserta una cadena de caracteres (tantos caracteres como quepan en la línea) "
"antes del carácter situado bajo el cursor, hasta *n* caracteres.   Si *n* es "
"cero o negativo, se inserta toda la cadena. Todos los caracteres situados a "
"la derecha del cursor se desplazan hacia la derecha, perdiéndose los "
"caracteres situados más a la derecha de la línea. La posición del cursor no "
"cambia (después de desplazarse a *y*, *x*, si se especifica)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1109
msgid ""
"Insert a character string (as many characters as will fit on the line) "
"before the character under the cursor.  All characters to the right of the "
"cursor are shifted right, with the rightmost characters on the line being "
"lost.  The cursor position does not change (after moving to *y*, *x*, if "
"specified)."
msgstr ""
"Inserta una cadena de caracteres (tantos como quepan en la línea) antes del "
"carácter situado bajo el cursor.  Todos los caracteres situados a la derecha "
"del cursor se desplazan hacia la derecha, perdiéndose los caracteres "
"situados más a la derecha de la línea.  La posición del cursor no cambia "
"(después de desplazarse a *y*, *x*, si se especifica)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1118
msgid ""
"Return a bytes object of characters, extracted from the window starting at "
"the current cursor position, or at *y*, *x* if specified, and stopping at "
"the end of the line. Attributes and color information are stripped from the "
"characters.  If *n* is specified, :meth:`instr` returns a string at most *n* "
"characters long (exclusive of the trailing NUL). The maximum value for *n* "
"is 2047."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1131
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the specified line was modified since the last call to :"
"meth:`refresh`; otherwise return ``False``.  Raise a :exc:`curses.error` "
"exception if *line* is not valid for the given window."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si la línea especificada fue modificada desde la última "
"llamada a :meth:`refresh`; en caso contrario devuelve ``False``.  Lanza una "
"excepción :exc:`curses.error` si *línea* no es válida para la ventana dada."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1138
msgid ""
"Return ``True`` if the specified window was modified since the last call to :"
"meth:`refresh`; otherwise return ``False``."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve ``True`` si la ventana especificada fue modificada desde la última "
"llamada a :meth:`refresh`; en caso contrario devuelve ``False``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1144
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, escape sequences generated by some keys (keypad,  "
"function keys) will be interpreted by :mod:`!curses`. If *flag* is "
"``False``, escape sequences will be left as is in the input stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1151
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, cursor is left where it is on update, instead of "
"being at \"cursor position.\"  This reduces cursor movement where possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1154
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``False``, cursor will always be at \"cursor position\" after "
"an update."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``False``, el cursor estará siempre en la \"posición del "
"cursor\" después de una actualización."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1159
msgid "Move cursor to ``(new_y, new_x)``."
msgstr "Mueva el cursor a ``(new_y, new_x)``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1164
msgid ""
"Move the window inside its parent window.  The screen-relative parameters of "
"the window are not changed.  This routine is used to display different parts "
"of the parent window at the same physical position on the screen."
msgstr ""
"Mueve la ventana dentro de su ventana padre.  Los parámetros relativos a la "
"pantalla de la ventana no se modifican.  Esta rutina se utiliza para mostrar "
"diferentes partes de la ventana padre en la misma posición física en la "
"pantalla."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1171
msgid "Move the window so its upper-left corner is at ``(new_y, new_x)``."
msgstr ""
"Mueva la ventana para que su esquina superior izquierda esté en ``(new_y, "
"new_x)``."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1173
msgid ""
"Moving the window so that any part of it would be off the screen is an "
"error: the window is not moved and :exc:`curses.error` is raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1179
msgid "If *flag* is ``True``, :meth:`getch` will be non-blocking."
msgstr "Si *flag* es ``True``, :meth:`getch` será no-bloqueante."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1184
msgid "If *flag* is ``True``, escape sequences will not be timed out."
msgstr "Si *flag* es ``True``, las secuencias de escape no serán temporizadas."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1186
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``False``, after a few milliseconds, an escape sequence will "
"not be interpreted, and will be left in the input stream as is."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``False``, después de unos milisegundos, una secuencia de "
"escape no será interpretada, y se dejará en el flujo de entrada tal cual."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1193
msgid ""
"Mark for refresh but wait.  This function updates the data structure "
"representing the desired state of the window, but does not force an update "
"of the physical screen.  To accomplish that, call  :func:`doupdate`."
msgstr ""
"Marcar para actualizar pero esperar.  Esta función actualiza la estructura "
"de datos que representa el estado deseado de la ventana, pero no fuerza una "
"actualización de la pantalla física.  Para ello, llame a :func:`doupdate`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1197
msgid ""
"The 6 arguments can only be specified, and are then required, when the "
"window is a pad created with :func:`newpad`; they have the same meaning as "
"for :meth:`refresh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1204
msgid ""
"Overlay the window on top of *destwin*. The windows need not be the same "
"size, only the overlapping region is copied. This copy is non-destructive, "
"which means that the current background character does not overwrite the old "
"contents of *destwin*."
msgstr ""
"Superpone la ventana sobre *destwin*. No es necesario que las ventanas "
"tengan el mismo tamaño, sólo se copia la región superpuesta. Esta copia no "
"es destructiva, lo que significa que el carácter de fondo actual no "
"sobrescribe el contenido antiguo de *destwin*."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1209
msgid ""
"To get fine-grained control over the copied region, the second form of :meth:"
"`overlay` can be used. *sminrow* and *smincol* are the upper-left "
"coordinates of the source window, and the other variables mark a rectangle "
"in the destination window."
msgstr ""
"Para obtener un control más preciso de la región copiada, puede utilizarse "
"la segunda forma de :meth:`overlay`. *sminrow* y *smincol* son las "
"coordenadas superiores izquierdas de la ventana de origen, y las otras "
"variables marcan un rectángulo en la ventana de destino."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1217
msgid ""
"Overwrite the window on top of *destwin*. The windows need not be the same "
"size, in which case only the overlapping region is copied. This copy is "
"destructive, which means that the current background character overwrites "
"the old contents of *destwin*."
msgstr ""
"Sobrescribe la ventana encima de *destwin*. No es necesario que las ventanas "
"tengan el mismo tamaño, en cuyo caso sólo se copia la región solapada. Esta "
"copia es destructiva, lo que significa que el carácter de fondo actual "
"sobrescribe el contenido antiguo de *destwin*."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1222
msgid ""
"To get fine-grained control over the copied region, the second form of :meth:"
"`overwrite` can be used. *sminrow* and *smincol* are the upper-left "
"coordinates of the source window, the other variables mark a rectangle in "
"the destination window."
msgstr ""
"Para obtener un control más preciso de la región copiada, puede utilizarse "
"la segunda forma de :meth:`overwrite`. *sminrow* y *smincol* son las "
"coordenadas superiores izquierdas de la ventana de origen, las otras "
"variables marcan un rectángulo en la ventana de destino."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1230
msgid ""
"Write all data associated with the window into the provided file object.  "
"This information can be later retrieved using the :func:`getwin` function."
msgstr ""
"Escribe todos los datos asociados a la ventana en el objeto de archivo "
"proporcionado.  Esta información puede recuperarse posteriormente mediante "
"la función :func:`getwin`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1236
msgid ""
"Indicate that the *num* screen lines, starting at line *beg*, are corrupted "
"and should be completely redrawn on the next :meth:`refresh` call."
msgstr ""
"Indica que las *num* líneas de pantalla, comenzando en la línea *beg*, están "
"corruptas y deben ser completamente redibujadas en la próxima llamada a :"
"meth:`refresh`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1242
msgid ""
"Touch the entire window, causing it to be completely redrawn on the next :"
"meth:`refresh` call."
msgstr ""
"Toca toda la ventana, haciendo que se redibuje completamente en la siguiente "
"llamada a :meth:`refresh`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1248
msgid ""
"Update the display immediately (sync actual screen with previous drawing/"
"deleting methods)."
msgstr ""
"Actualiza la pantalla inmediatamente (sincroniza la pantalla real con los "
"métodos de dibujo/borrado anteriores)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1251
msgid ""
"The 6 arguments can only be specified, and are then required, when the "
"window is a pad created with :func:`newpad`.  The additional parameters are "
"needed to indicate what part of the pad and screen are involved. *pminrow* "
"and *pmincol* specify the upper-left corner of the rectangle to be displayed "
"in the pad.  *sminrow*, *smincol*, *smaxrow*, and *smaxcol* specify the "
"edges of the rectangle to be displayed on the screen.  The lower-right "
"corner of the rectangle to be displayed in the pad is calculated from the "
"screen coordinates, since the rectangles must be the same size.  Both "
"rectangles must be entirely contained within their respective structures.  "
"Negative values of *pminrow*, *pmincol*, *sminrow*, or *smincol* are treated "
"as if they were zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1265
msgid ""
"Reallocate storage for a curses window to adjust its dimensions to the "
"specified values.  If either dimension is larger than the current values, "
"the window's data is filled with blanks that have the current background "
"rendition (as set by :meth:`bkgdset`) merged into them."
msgstr ""
"Reasigna el almacenamiento de una ventana curses para ajustar sus "
"dimensiones a los valores especificados.  Si cualquiera de las dimensiones "
"es mayor que los valores actuales, los datos de la ventana se rellenan con "
"espacios en blanco que tienen la representación de fondo actual (según lo "
"establecido por :meth:`bkgdset`) fusionada en ellos."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1273
msgid ""
"Scroll the screen or scrolling region.  Scroll upward by *lines* lines if "
"*lines* is positive, or downward if it is negative.  Scrolling has no effect "
"unless it has been enabled for the window with :meth:`scrollok`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1280
msgid ""
"Control what happens when the cursor of a window is moved off the edge of "
"the window or scrolling region, either as a result of a newline action on "
"the bottom line, or typing the last character of the last line.  If *flag* "
"is ``False``, the cursor is left on the bottom line.  If *flag* is ``True``, "
"the window is scrolled up one line.  Note that in order to get the physical "
"scrolling effect on the terminal, it is also necessary to call :meth:`idlok`."
msgstr ""
"Controla lo que ocurre cuando el cursor de una ventana se desplaza fuera del "
"borde de la ventana o de la región de desplazamiento, ya sea como resultado "
"de una acción de nueva línea en la línea inferior, o tecleando el último "
"carácter de la última línea.  Si *flag* es ``False``, el cursor se deja en "
"la línea inferior.  Si *flag* es ``True``, la ventana se desplaza una línea "
"hacia arriba.  Tenga en cuenta que para obtener el efecto de desplazamiento "
"físico en el terminal, también es necesario llamar a :meth:`idlok`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1290
msgid ""
"Set the scrolling region from line *top* to line *bottom*. All scrolling "
"actions will take place in this region."
msgstr ""
"Establece la región de desplazamiento desde la línea *superior* hasta la "
"línea *inferior*. Todas las acciones de desplazamiento tendrán lugar en esta "
"región."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1296
msgid ""
"Turn off the standout attribute.  On some terminals this has the side effect "
"of turning off all attributes."
msgstr ""
"Desactivar el atributo destacado.  En algunos terminales esto tiene el "
"efecto secundario de desactivar todos los atributos."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1302
msgid "Turn on attribute *A_STANDOUT*."
msgstr "Activa el atributo *A_STANDOUT*."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1308
msgid ""
"Return a sub-pad, whose upper-left corner is at ``(begin_y, begin_x)``, and "
"whose width/height is *ncols*/*nlines*.  The coordinates are relative to the "
"parent pad (unlike :meth:`subwin`, which uses screen coordinates).  This "
"method is only available for pads created with :func:`newpad`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1317
msgid ""
"Return a sub-window, whose upper-left corner is at the screen-relative "
"coordinates ``(begin_y, begin_x)``, and whose width/height is *ncols*/"
"*nlines*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1320
msgid ""
"By default, the sub-window will extend from the specified position to the "
"lower right corner of the window."
msgstr ""
"Por defecto, la subventana se extenderá desde la posición especificada hasta "
"la esquina inferior derecha de la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1326
msgid ""
"Touch each location in the window that has been touched in any of its "
"ancestor windows.  This routine is called by :meth:`refresh`, so it should "
"almost never be necessary to call it manually."
msgstr ""
"Toca cada lugar de la ventana que haya sido tocado en cualquiera de sus "
"ventanas antecesoras.  Esta rutina es llamada por :meth:`refresh`, por lo "
"que casi nunca debería ser necesario llamarla manualmente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1333
msgid ""
"If *flag* is ``True``, then :meth:`syncup` is called automatically whenever "
"there is a change in the window."
msgstr ""
"Si *flag* es ``True``, entonces se llama :meth:`syncup` de forma automática "
"cada vez que hay un cambio en la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1339
msgid ""
"Touch all locations in ancestors of the window that have been changed in  "
"the window."
msgstr ""
"Toque todas las ubicaciones en los ancestros de la ventana que se han "
"cambiado en la ventana."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1345
msgid ""
"Set blocking or non-blocking read behavior for the window.  If *delay* is "
"negative, blocking read is used (which will wait indefinitely for input).  "
"If *delay* is zero, then non-blocking read is used, and :meth:`getch` will "
"return ``-1`` if no input is waiting.  If *delay* is positive, then :meth:"
"`getch` will block for *delay* milliseconds, and return ``-1`` if there is "
"still no input at the end of that time."
msgstr ""
"Establece el comportamiento de lectura bloqueante o no bloqueante para la "
"ventana.  Si *delay* es negativo, se utiliza lectura de bloqueo (que "
"esperará indefinidamente la entrada).  Si *delay* es cero, entonces se usa "
"lectura no bloqueante, y :meth:`getch` devolverá ``-1`` si no hay entrada "
"esperando.  Si *delay* es positivo, entonces :meth:`getch` se bloqueará "
"durante *delay* milisegundos, y devolverá ``-1`` si todavía no hay entrada "
"al final de ese tiempo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1355
msgid ""
"Pretend *count* lines have been changed, starting with line *start*.  If "
"*changed* is supplied, it specifies whether the affected lines are marked as "
"having been changed (*changed*\\ ``=True``) or unchanged (*changed*\\ "
"``=False``)."
msgstr ""
"Pretende que se han cambiado *count*, empezando por la línea *start*.  Si se "
"proporciona *changed*, se especifica si las líneas afectadas se marcan como "
"cambiadas (*changed*\\ ``=True``) o no cambiadas (*changed*\\ ``=False``)."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1362
msgid ""
"Pretend the whole window has been changed, for purposes of drawing "
"optimizations."
msgstr ""
"Fingir que se ha cambiado toda la ventana, a efectos de optimizaciones de "
"dibujo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1368
msgid ""
"Mark all lines in  the  window  as unchanged since the last call to :meth:"
"`refresh`."
msgstr ""
"Marca todas las líneas de la ventana como no modificadas desde la última "
"llamada a :meth:`refresh`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1375
msgid ""
"Display a vertical line starting at ``(y, x)`` with length *n* consisting of "
"the character *ch* with attributes *attr*."
msgstr ""
"Muestra una línea vertical que comienza en ``(y, x)`` con longitud *n* "
"formada por el carácter *ch* con atributos *attr*."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1380
msgid "Constants"
msgstr "Constantes"

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1382
msgid "The :mod:`!curses` module defines the following data members:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1387
msgid ""
"Some curses routines  that  return  an integer, such as :meth:`~window."
"getch`, return :const:`ERR` upon failure."
msgstr ""
"Algunas rutinas curses que devuelven un entero, como :meth:`~window.getch`, "
"devuelven :const:`ERR` en caso de fallo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1393
msgid ""
"Some curses routines  that  return  an integer, such as  :func:`napms`, "
"return :const:`OK` upon success."
msgstr ""
"Algunas rutinas curses que devuelven un entero, como :func:`napms`, "
"devuelven :const:`OK` en caso de éxito."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1399
msgid "A bytes object representing the current version of the module."
msgstr "Un objeto bytes que representa la versión actual del módulo."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1404
msgid ""
"A named tuple containing the three components of the ncurses library "
"version: *major*, *minor*, and *patch*.  All values are integers.  The "
"components can also be accessed by name,  so ``curses.ncurses_version[0]`` "
"is equivalent to ``curses.ncurses_version.major`` and so on."
msgstr ""
"Una tupla con nombre que contiene los tres componentes de la versión de la "
"biblioteca ncurses: *major*, *minor*, y *patch*.  Todos los valores son "
"enteros.  Los componentes también se pueden acceder por nombre, así que "
"``curses.ncurses_version[0]`` es equivalente a ``curses.ncurses_version."
"major`` y así sucesivamente."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1409
msgid "Availability: if the ncurses library is used."
msgstr "Disponibilidad: si se utiliza la biblioteca ncurses."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1415
msgid ""
"The maximum number of colors the terminal can support. It is defined only "
"after the call to :func:`start_color`."
msgstr ""
"El número máximo de colores que puede admitir el terminal. Se define sólo "
"después de la llamada a :func:`start_color`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1420
msgid ""
"The maximum number of color pairs the terminal can support. It is defined "
"only after the call to :func:`start_color`."
msgstr ""
"El número máximo de pares de colores que puede admitir el terminal. Se "
"define sólo después de la llamada a :func:`start_color`."

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1425
msgid ""
"The width of the screen, that is, the number of columns. It is defined only "
"after the call to :func:`initscr`. Updated by :func:`update_lines_cols`, :"
"func:`resizeterm` and :func:`resize_term`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/curses.rst:1432
msgid ""
"The height of the screen, that is, the number of lines. It is defined only "
"after the call to :func:`initscr`. Updated by :func:`update_lines_cols`, :"
"func:`resizeterm` and :func:`resize_term`."
msgstr ""

